      "message_categories": ["transactional", "operational"],
      "applicability": "A robotext to a wireless number. 47 CFR 64.1200 reaches it as a 'call'; the telephone-solicitation provisions do not, because this content does not encourage a purchase.",
      "requirements": {
        "consent_standard": {
          "value": "express",
          "basis_kind": "statute_requires",
          "enforced_by": "send-gate",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
          "citations": ["cfr-64.1200-a1"],
          "basis_citation": "cfr-64.1200-a1",
          "note": "(a)(1) conditions the prohibition on the call being made with an automatic telephone dialing system or an artificial or prerecorded voice. Whether this platform is an ATDS is a contested legal question we do not resolve here.",
          "architecture_note": "The gate requires a granted consent row for consumer recipients whatever the answer to the ATDS question is (requiresExpressSmsConsent). That is a posture, not a reading of the regulation.",
          "open_question": "Post-Facebook v. Duguid, is this platform's send path an ATDS? Not answered; the conservative posture above makes the answer non-load-bearing for whether we send."
        },
        "quiet_hours": {
          "value": "not_applicable",
          "basis_kind": "statute_scope",
          "enforced_by": "send-gate",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
          "citations": ["cfr-64.1200-c1", "cfr-64.1200-f15", "cfr-64.1200-e", "ca-state-quiet-hours"],
          // The DEFINITION, not the duty: what makes the restriction inapplicable
          // here is (f)(15)'s scope, so that is the text this value rests on.
          "basis_citation": "cfr-64.1200-f15",
          "note": "The 8 a.m.-9 p.m. restriction is imposed on a 'telephone solicitation', which (f)(15) defines as a call or message for the purpose of encouraging a purchase, rental or investment. A booking confirmation or a report-ready notice is not one, so the restriction never attaches. This is the provision's SCOPE, not an exemption granted to us and not a fact about our architecture.",
          "open_question": "No California-specific calling-hours statute was located for SMS; Bus. & Prof. Code art. 8 (17590-17594) is a do-not-call scheme. See the `ca-state-quiet-hours` citation, which is unverified."
        },
        "identification": {
          "value": "required",
          "basis_kind": "product_posture",
          "enforced_by": "sender-identity",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
          "citations": ["ctia-messaging-principles"],
          "basis_citation": "ctia-messaging-principles",
          "note": "64.1200(b)'s identification duty is written for artificial or prerecorded voice messages, so no federal provision read here imposes sender identification on a transactional SMS. We record it as required anyway, and say plainly that the source is industry guidance nobody here has read rather than a statute.",
          "architecture_note": "resolveSmsSenderIdentity records the platform sender and the tenant on whose behalf the message went out (counsel 26a-3). That is a RECORD of identification, which is not the same as identifying the sender inside the message body.",
          "open_question": "Is there a US provision - federal or California - that requires sender identification inside a transactional SMS body, or is CTIA guidance the only source? Until that is read, this value is our own posture and must not be cited as law."
        },
        "unsubscribe": {
          "value": "required",
          "basis_kind": "statute_requires",
          "enforced_by": "inbound-stop-webhook",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
          "citations": ["cfr-64.1200-a10"],
          "basis_citation": "cfr-64.1200-a10",
          "note": "The FCC's revocation rules are the authority and they have NOT been read. The requirement is recorded as required because we already honour STOP unconditionally, so nothing about the product waits on the reading.",
          "architecture_note": "Inbound STOP is recorded as a revocation in server/api/sms.ts and the send gate refuses on the latest revoked row for every purpose, including test sends.",
          "open_question": "Read 47 CFR 64.1200(a)(10) and the 2024 revocation order, then replace the unverified citation."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "country": "US",
      "region": "CA",
      "label": "United States - California",
      "channel": "sms",
      "message_categories": ["marketing"],
      "applicability": "A text message to a wireless number encouraging a purchase, rental or investment - a 'telephone solicitation' under (f)(15) and 'telemarketing' under (f)(13).",
      "requirements": {
        "consent_standard": {
          "value": "express_written",
          "basis_kind": "statute_requires",
          "enforced_by": "send-gate",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
