          "basis_citation": "cfr-64.1200-a2",
          "note": "(a)(2) demands prior express WRITTEN consent for a call that includes or introduces an advertisement or constitutes telemarketing, and (f)(9) defines that as an agreement in writing bearing the signature of the person called. The consent this product holds was captured under a disclosure describing appointment and report updates; it is not that agreement.",
          "architecture_note": "Marketing is refused on this channel outright, by content variable and by class category, before any jurisdiction rule is consulted (counsel 26a-2, option (a)). The refusal is a product decision, not a reading that the statute forbids the message."
        },
