          "note": "6(2)(a) requires prescribed information identifying the sender AND the person on whose behalf the message is sent where different, and 6(2)(b) requires contact information the recipient can readily use. This is owed even where 6(6) excuses consent, which is the half of our earlier reading counsel called too wide. A phone number alone does not discharge it.",
          "architecture_note": "The two-role record exists (resolveSmsSenderIdentity: platform sender plus tenant on whose behalf). What is NOT proven is that the message BODY carries the prescribed identification and contact information.",
