          "note": "6(2)(c) requires an unsubscribe mechanism conforming to 11(1); 11(2) requires the address or page in 11(1)(b) to stay valid for a minimum of 60 days after the message is sent; 11(3) requires effect to be given without delay and no later than 10 business days.",
          "architecture_note": "Reply STOP is our mechanism and it is processed on receipt, which satisfies 11(3)'s outer limit by construction rather than by a job. That CRTC accepts STOP as a mechanism is counsel's citation and is recorded as a secondary source."
