      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-6.html",
      "quote": "The message must be in a form that conforms to the prescribed requirements and must (a) set out prescribed information that identifies the person who sent the message and the person - if different - on whose behalf it is sent; (b) set out information enabling the person to whom the message is sent to readily contact one of the persons referred to in paragraph (a); and (c) set out an unsubscribe mechanism in accordance with subsection 11(1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "casl-6-6",
      "authority": "CASL s. 6(6)",
      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-6.html",
      "quote": "Paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to a commercial electronic message that solely [(a) provides a quote or estimate for the supply of a product or service, if the quote or estimate was requested; (b) facilitates, completes or confirms a commercial transaction that the person to whom the message is sent previously agreed to enter into; (c) provides warranty, product recall, or safety or security information; (d) provides factual information about a subscription, membership, account, loan or similar ongoing relationship; (e) provides information about an employment relationship or benefit plan; (f) delivers a product, goods or a service, including product updates or upgrades; or (g) communicates a purpose specified in the regulations]"
    },
    {
      "id": "casl-10-9",
      "authority": "CASL s. 10(9)",
      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-10.html",
      "quote": "consent is implied only if ... (a) the person who sends the message, the person who causes it to be sent or the person who permits it to be sent has an existing business relationship or an existing non-business relationship with the person to whom it is sent"
    },
    {
      "id": "casl-11-1",
      "authority": "CASL s. 11(1)",
      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-11.html",
      "quote": "(a) enable the person to whom the commercial electronic message is sent to indicate, at no cost to them, the wish to no longer receive any commercial electronic messages ... (b) specify an electronic address, or link to a page on the World Wide Web that can be accessed through a web browser, to which the indication may be sent"
    },
    {
      "id": "casl-11-2",
      "authority": "CASL s. 11(2)",
      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-11.html",
      "quote": "the electronic address or World Wide Web page referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is valid for a minimum of 60 days after the message has been sent."
    },
    {
      "id": "casl-11-3",
      "authority": "CASL s. 11(3)",
      "verified_against": "primary_text",
      "checked_on": "2026-08-17",
      "source": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-1.6/section-11.html",
      "quote": "effect is given to an indication sent in accordance with paragraph (1)(b) without delay, and in any event no later than 10 business days after the indication has been sent."
